    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bc8aea02_c36c5387",
        "filename": "core/minute-ia/task.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 274,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137654
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-14T06:36:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For me(although I\u0027m new to ECOS), it looks like \"svc_call\" is for counting synchronous exception so I think it should be moved to __swicth_to in switch.S in our case.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 273,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 274,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "fab6e11dc218563fdc615f5c97cf53ee8b93b49b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8c68296b_3b62ef70",
        "filename": "core/minute-ia/task.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 274,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-15T23:20:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see it as the number of times a register IRQ was called.\nThe unregistered IRQ count is lost (but it does print to the console since it is unexpected)\nThe number of switchto call is instrumented through task_switches variable. \n\nThat should cover all of the cases since switchto and default_int_handler are the only irq that don\u0027t go through task_start_irq_handler",
      "parentUuid": "bc8aea02_c36c5387",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 273,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 274,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "fab6e11dc218563fdc615f5c97cf53ee8b93b49b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "429a440a_5601031f",
        "filename": "core/minute-ia/task.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 274,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137654
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-01-16T00:50:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For me, it looks like\n\n- \"task_switches\" is for counting number of actual task switches. Not all __switchto calls increase the number of \"task_switches\".\n\n- most of all, svc_calls is about to count synchronous exceptions. For now, we only have one normal synchronous exception(__switchto). Other synchronous exceptions are for error cases(fetch, aborts \u0027\u0027\u0027) and we are not handling them.\n\nAnyway, according to the implementation of \"taskinfo\", \"Total exceptions \u003d all irqs + svc_call\" which means \"asynchronous exceptions(total irqs) + synchronous exception(svc_call)\".\n\nSo I believe it should be moved to __switch_to in \"switch.S\".",
      "parentUuid": "8c68296b_3b62ef70",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 273,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 274,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "fab6e11dc218563fdc615f5c97cf53ee8b93b49b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
